{% assign smart__StructureDefinition__KGProgramIndicator__elements__description = "DAK component 7. Named program-indicator and not `indicator` because L1 already declares an `indicator` -- one normatively defined in a publication. They are different things: this is the DAK's operational measure, and `derivedFrom` is how it points at the normative one. Collapsing them would silently merge a WHO definition with a country's implementation of it. numerator, denominator and disaggregation are all `1..1 markdown` -- prose, not a computable expression. Nothing here should be read as a calculable measure; the L3 FHIR Measure is where that would live. resolutionStatus is `unresolved` on a component that something else names but no DAK declares -- an L3 artefact whose title carries the component id, for instance. The node exists so the gap is queryable and carries the referenced id and nothing else. Class IRI: http://smart.who.int/kg/program-indicator." %}
